# Visualization Concept — Productive / Cognitive Enhancement / Part 1.1: Signal and Noise

> **Style lock:** Productive pillar · Cognitive Enhancement track · the locked **"Neural Signal Schematic"** style (ink-black field, thin glowing cyan traces, instrument-grade JetBrains-Mono labels, single-alarm-color discipline, the mind rendered as a signal/power schematic — never a glowing brain). This is the 6th Cognitive concept. Where **1.0 was the unpopulated master blueprint** (the legend every other poster reads from), **1.1 is the first OPERATING instrument in the set** — it takes exactly one region of that board (the **EXCITATION ↔ INHIBITION / gas ↔ brakes spine** plus the **Flexibility socket**) and switches it ON so you can watch the mechanism run. The 1.0 note said every later Cognitive poster is "a zoom-in on one region of this board"; this is that zoom-in, made live.

